he volume of the finite region\n# The region of interest is defined by x < y < z and x + y + z = 75\n# We can express z in terms of x and y using the plane equation\nz_expr = 75 - x - y\n\n# Integrate over the region where x < y < z and x + y + z = 75\nvolume = sp.integrate(1, (z, 0, 75 - x - y), (y, 0, 75 - x), (x, 0, 75))\n\n# Simplify the volume expression\nvolume = sp.simplify(volume)\n\n# Express the volume in the form a*sqrt(b)\na, b = sp.fraction(volume)\n\n# Calculate a + b\nresult = a + b\nprint(result)\n```\n```output\n8850\n```\nThe area of the finite region can be expressed in the form \\( a\\sqrt{b} \\), where \\( a \\) and \\( b \\) are positive integers and \\( b \\) is not divisible by the square of any prime. From the output, we have \\( a = 8850 \\) and \\( b = 1 \\).\n\nTherefore, \\( a + b = 8850 + 1 = 8851 \\).\n\nThe final answer is \\(\\boxed{8851}\\).",
